From 1d240bf4f1fe314a6e4bfa4f4cca2a3403b6f1e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Floyd Everest <me@floydeverest.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:09:17 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Dev Containers: run initializeCommand on the host

initializeCommand was never run: the terminal build script omits it, and
the vendored CLI code that handles it (runInitializeCommand via
resolve/launch) is unreachable.

Run it on the host in the workspace folder, as the spec requires, both
when building (as the first step of the build script, before the image is
built or the container created) and when reusing an existing container
(spawned before the container is started, with output in the Dev
Containers log). String commands go through sh -c / cmd /c, array
commands run without a shell, and object commands run each entry in turn.
A non-zero exit fails the build or aborts the reopen.

The devcontainer.json lookup, parsing and variable substitution move out
of buildAndCreate into loadDevContainerConfig() so both paths share them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FZKDAdw2eAGaetRMyaR7xv
